        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    xyz_returns = [0.025, -0.012, 0.038, 0.017, 0.040]\n    market_returns = [0.018, -0.005, 0.021, 0.013, 0.035]\n\n    # Do math calculation to get the answer\n    xyz_mean = sum(xyz_returns) / len(xyz_returns)\n    market_mean = sum(market_returns) / len(market_returns)\n\n    covariance = sum(\n        (xyz - xyz_mean) * (market - market_mean)\n        for xyz, market in zip(xyz_returns, market_returns)\n    )\n\n    market_variance = sum(\n        (market - market_mean) ** 2\n        for market in market_returns\n    )\n\n    beta = covariance / market_variance\n    answer = round(beta, 2)\n\n    # return answer\n    return answer\n```",
